<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:51:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nearly 1,600 migrants arrive on Spain's Canary Islands in one day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8f63803415ac25da71dfba4a0462383f453c9787c28fe36a7d00bb9e2423be</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941--709bffa2c1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The majority of the migrants who arrived on the islands on Saturday came from Senegal, Gambia, and Guinea. The surge in arrivals to the Canaries comes after Spain's Ceuta recently faced a migration crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cape Verde election: Jose Maria Neves set to win second term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db6132e52c6d6a427cbd4d8b58e64815e2efcab12c365b41af1a474c6f4986e6</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:51:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cape-verde-election-jose-maria-neves-set-to-win-second-term/a-79952606--b48b9d9ee543.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cape-verde-election-jose-maria-neves-set-to-win-second-term/a-79952606?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly two-thirds of the voters in the West African nation voted to keep President Jose Maria Neves in office, according to provisional results.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges unity as Francophonie summit opens in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fed1687e8f47eebdedbce00cc3c438eb01380104248f6d1f8d3b24715237edb</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201--02576530ba13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaders of French-speaking nations gathered in Phnom Penh as a row over who should lead the Francophonie and Congo’s threat to quit put pressure on Macron to broker consensus.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20672002626114fba9573e25626b1a4cdc0642454d19ccc5aacedec002b53bcf</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a9f3d5e84ef4570563b7e229b4af6215519f7d2b4af2842418eaf4bc2793da0</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
